# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOBO — environment
# Copy to .env.local. Never commit the real file; .env* is gitignored.
# Every value here is read on the server only and never reaches the browser
# (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — that prefix would inline the value into the bundle).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- WordPress CRM ---------------------------------------------------------
# mobo.md already runs WordPress, so the CRM most likely lives there.
# Create an Application Password:  WP Admin > Users > Profile > Application Passwords
# Use HTTPS only — Basic auth over plain HTTP sends the password in clear text.
#
# Custom endpoint:
#   WP_CRM_ENDPOINT="https://cms.mobo.md/wp-json/mobo/v1/leads"
# FluentCRM:
#   WP_CRM_ENDPOINT="https://cms.mobo.md/wp-json/fluent-crm/v2/subscribers"
WP_CRM_ENDPOINT=""
WP_CRM_USER=""
WP_CRM_APP_PASSWORD=""

# --- Telegram notification (optional) --------------------------------------
# Pings the sales team the moment a lead lands. Create a bot with @BotFather.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=""
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=""

# With none of the above set, the form still works end to end and leads are
# written to the server log by the console provider.
